import{_ as t,o as a,c as i,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.BUOFcz_J.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Native tools, with Core selected when needed","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"records/native-tools-episode.md","filePath":"records/native-tools-episode.md"}'),o={name:"records/native-tools-episode.md"};function s(r,e,c,d,l,p){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<div class="warning custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">Historical record</p><p>This page records what happened on a date, with its observed failures and limits. It is not a requirement for the current implementation. Current behaviour is in <a href="/Rho/docs/reference/status">Status</a>.</p></div><h1 id="native-tools-with-core-selected-when-needed" tabindex="-1">Native tools, with Core selected when needed <a class="header-anchor" href="#native-tools-with-core-selected-when-needed" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Native tools, with Core selected when needed&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Updated: 2026-10-29. The user selected this change after the <a href="/Rho/docs/records/core-value-episode">corrected Iris comparison</a>.</p><h2 id="what-changed" tabindex="-1">What changed <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-changed" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What changed&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The comparison retained its measurements and original protocol. Its assertions that a Python executor cannot launch compiled programs, that Rho cannot execute arbitrary R, and that the small shell helper supplies equivalent guarantees were corrected. The measured language choices and timings do not isolate Core&#39;s causal effect. Output spooling remains a plausible cost, not an isolated benchmark.</p><p>Agents normally use native tools under their existing permissions. Core managed execution is chosen when a concrete operation needs continuity or a retained application record. Activity observation and honest partial/unknown facts remain.</p><ul><li>The compatibility Claude CLI driver no longer passes <code>--tools &#39;&#39;</code>, <code>--strict-mcp-config</code> or <code>--permission-mode dontAsk</code>. It keeps native tools, configured MCP servers and native permission settings. The existing project grant still covers only the four Rho MCP tools. No permission bypass was added. Its noninteractive entry cannot answer a new native permission request; ACP continues to offer those choices in the application.</li><li>ACP already exposed native tools; its execution and permission paths are unchanged by this work. MCP discovery and the managed R skill now explain that these workspace capabilities supplement native tools.</li><li>The default launcher can start without a discovered Core binary. A bad explicit selection or invalid bundled artifact is still an error. A missing Core is reported when managed execution or Host activity is selected; no alternate run is substituted. General project diagnosis treats missing R as an optional-entry warning; the managed <code>run-r</code> intent still requires its prerequisites.</li><li>Existing managed requests, output, cancellation facts and unknown outcomes keep their behavior. Native actions do not gain managed acceptance, deduplication or scientific validity merely by being observed.</li><li>The three owners&#39; development guidance now makes this execution choice explicit. Dependency direction and identity-generation location are reviewable mechanisms; existing accepted identities and honest facts remain protected.</li></ul><h2 id="checks-and-actual-result" tabindex="-1">Checks and actual result <a class="header-anchor" href="#checks-and-actual-result" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Checks and actual result&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Evidence is retained in <code>work/native-tools-20261029/</code> in the Rho checkout.</p><ul><li>Agent and R plugin TypeScript builds passed; application service and web builds passed. The focused runtime, diagnosis and compatibility-conversation checks passed 11/11. The complete serial application suite passed 223/223; the plugin suite passed 104/104, including retained activity and execution consumers.</li><li>New checks cover missing optional Core, rejection of a missing explicitly selected binary, native output visible in Documents without a managed record, absence of a Host, and unchanged missing-prerequisite handling for managed work. The compatibility process fixture checks that Rho neither disables native tools nor supplies a permission override; original conversation recovery remains covered.</li><li>A real Claude CLI conversation, using the existing test model <code>westlakehpc/deepseek-v4.1-flash</code>, ran <code>node native-probe.cjs</code> with native Bash in a disposable project. The script compiled a small C program and ran it. The retained reply and the actual file contained <code>NATIVE_C_OK</code>; no Core binary was configured, no Host socket appeared, and no application operation was created. A temporary native settings file allowed only that exact test command; no user settings or credentials were changed. The owned service and project were removed.</li><li>Chrome opened the project and Agent panel without Core. Initial screenshots caught loading/new-conversation state; the follow-up waited for the loaded project and selected the retained answer. The desktop (1440 × 900) and narrow (390 × 844) screenshots were inspected: the native command, answer and input are visible; no browser errors were reported. This is a functional check, not a usability study.</li><li>Documentation checks found no broken local links or anchors in 290 references. All 64 rendered browser pages were inspected, including the two status snapshots prepared for commit without unrelated edits. Later wording fixes were rerendered and affected pages checked; unchanged observations were reused.</li></ul><p>Initial test failures were retained: one new fixture embedded a literal newline in JavaScript, one read <code>text</code> instead of Documents&#39; <code>content</code>, and an older diagnosis assertion still treated optional R as a global failure. These were corrected and the affected checks passed before the complete suite ran.</p><h2 id="scope" tabindex="-1">Scope <a class="header-anchor" href="#scope" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Scope&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This is a source-working-tree check alongside unrelated ongoing changes; it is not an accepted clean package composition, installation or release. No user Host or R session was restarted. Core execution code and its compiled contract documents were not changed, so Cargo checks were not rerun. Existing managed-only acceptance cases still test their explicitly selected path; they do not prescribe an Agent default. Output coalescing, revised log completeness and snapshot path semantics remain separate work. The original Iris experiment was not rerun or regraded.</p>',13)])])}const m=t(o,[["render",s]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
